{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS64amdfA5abuc2xzD2t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my exploration of the repository, here is my analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n1. **Order entity** (`Order.kt:11`): Currently lacks a status field; has orderId, customerId, amount, currency\n2. **OrderController** (`OrderController.kt:15-43`): Has POST/GET /orders endpoints; uses ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) \n3. **Shipment entity** (`Shipment.kt:9`): Already has status enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n4. **ShipmentRepository** (`ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`): Only supports find by shipmentId, not by orderId—will need a method to find shipments by order\n5. **ShipmentController** (`ShipmentController.kt:26-43`): Creates shipments without checking order status\n6. **API error handling** (`ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`, `ApiError.kt:31-37`): Uses sealed exception classes; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError responses\n7. **ErrorCode enum** (`ApiError.kt:31`): Has ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n\n**Conventions this repository uses:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler handles the response envelope\n- 404 for ResourceNotFoundException, 409 for ConflictException, 201 for created resources\n- In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions, testing both success and error response bodies\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` – Add OrderStatus enum and status field\n2. `OrderController.kt` – Add POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with atomicity and idempotency logic\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` – Add findByOrderId() method to support batch operations\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` – Validate that target order is ACTIVE when creating shipments\n5. `ApiError.kt` – Add ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` – Add tests for cancel endpoint (success, idempotency, conflict, not found)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Atomicity: Cancelling must check all shipments before updating any, or one shipment status update could leave the order in an inconsistent state\n- The shipment-finding loop and order update are not transactional in an in-memory store\n- ShipmentRepository must support finding multiple shipments by orderId\n\n**Open questions:** None; the requirements are specific enough.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** – Add `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to the Order data class.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** – Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method that:\n   - Fetches the order; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it (idempotency)\n   - Load all shipments for that order\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT code; do NOT modify anything\n   - Otherwise, update order status to CANCELLED and all shipments with status CREATED to CANCELLED\n   - Return the updated order with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** – Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** – In the create method, after validating the shipment doesn't already exist, check that the order exists and is ACTIVE. If the order exists but is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** – Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** – Add four new tests:\n   - Cancel ACTIVE order succeeds, order is CANCELLED, and CREATED shipments are cancelled\n   - Repeated cancel of CANCELLED order succeeds and changes nothing\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409, no changes\n   - Cancel of non-existent order returns 404\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered creating a separate OrderService class to handle the cancel logic and shipment updates, but given the in-memory repositories and existing controller-level validation, keeping the logic in the controller (calling repository methods directly) is simpler and matches the existing pattern where OrderController directly calls repository.save().\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments**:\n  - Request: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n  - Controller calls `repository.findById(\"O-1\")`\n  - Controller calls `shipmentRepository.findByOrderId(\"O-1\")`\n  - No CONFIRMED found → proceed\n  - Update order in repository (status CANCELLED)\n  - For each CREATED shipment, update it to CANCELLED in repository\n  - Response: 200 OK, Order with status CANCELLED\n\n- **Repeated cancel**:\n  - Request: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n  - Controller calls `repository.findById(\"O-1\")`\n  - Status is already CANCELLED → return immediately\n  - Response: 200 OK, Order with status CANCELLED\n\n- **Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment**:\n  - Request: `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`\n  - Controller calls `repository.findById(\"O-1\")`\n  - Controller calls `shipmentRepository.findByOrderId(\"O-1\")`\n  - CONFIRMED shipment found → throw ConflictException(\"ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\", ...)\n  - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 409 Conflict\n  - Order and all shipments unchanged in repository\n\n- **Cancel non-existent order**:\n  - Request: `POST /orders/O-missing/cancel`\n  - Controller calls `repository.findById(\"O-missing\")`\n  - Returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException(\"ORDER_NOT_FOUND\", ...)\n  - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 404 Not Found\n\n- **Create shipment for CANCELLED order**:\n  - Request: `POST /shipments` with orderId for cancelled order\n  - Controller checks `orderRepository.findById(request.orderId)`\n  - Status is CANCELLED → throw ConflictException(\"ORDER_CANCELLED\", ...)\n  - GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 409 Conflict\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order** – Create order O-1, create shipment S-1 in CREATED, cancel O-1, verify order status is CANCELLED and shipment status is CANCELLED\n2. **Idempotent cancel** – Create order O-2, cancel it, cancel it again, verify second cancel returns 200 and nothing changed\n3. **Conflict: CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel** – Create order O-3, create shipment S-3, manually update shipment to CONFIRMED (via repository), attempt cancel, verify 409 response and no changes to order or shipments\n4. **Not found** – Attempt cancel of non-existent order, verify 404 response\n5. **Create shipment for cancelled order** – Create order O-4, cancel it, attempt to create shipment for O-4, verify 409 response\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1519,"cache_read_input_tokens":20373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1519},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5549515-9791-4935-9265-1d8e40a7d5df","uuid":"ac5bcdf8-645d-4c41-9789-98b6656e5337","timestamp":"2026-09-26T12:56:57.961Z","request_id":"req_011CfS64aQ4XoGVRMoNh1W7K"}
