nt)\n   - ShipmentController.kt (added order validation)\n   - ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId method)\n   - ApiError.kt (added error codes)\n   - OrderControllerTest.kt (added tests)\n   - ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added orderRepository injection/clearing)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt**: Added OrderStatus enum and status field with proper default—necessary for order lifecycle\n- **OrderController.kt**: Added shipmentRepository injection and cancel endpoint—necessary for cancellation logic\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added orderRepository injection and validation—necessary to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Added findByOrderId method—necessary to find shipments belonging to an order during cancellation\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added two new error codes—necessary for proper error reporting\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Added 4 new tests covering all cancel scenarios and injected shipmentRepository—necessary for verification\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added orderRepository injection and clearing—necessary to prevent test pollution across test classes\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint to cancel orders atomically, with idempotency, and prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum and status field to track order lifecycle\n              OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with atomicity check (CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel)\n              ShipmentController.kt — added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId method to support cancellation logic\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 5 tests covering cancel scenarios (active order, repeated cancel, conflict, not found, shipment creation blocking)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added orderRepository injection to clear state between tests\n\nTests         cancels an active order with created shipments — verifies order and shipments transition to CANCELLED\n              repeated cancel of already cancelled order succeeds — verifies idempotency\n              cancel fails with 409 if any shipment is confirmed — verifies atomicity: no partial updates on conflict\n              cancel of non-existent order returns 404 — verifies error handling\n              creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409 — verifies shipment creation blocking for cancelled orders\n\nVerification  ./mvnw test — all 18 tests pass (9 OrderControllerTest including 5 new, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, 5 ShipmentControllerTest, 3 CustomerControllerTest)\n\nNot done      none\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2299,"cache_read_input_tokens":55434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2299},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5549515-9791-4935-9265-1d8e40a7d5df","uuid":"e68d0c49-6296-4f61-8119-f9ceced384e0","timestamp":"2026-09-26T12:59:48.696Z","request_id":"req_011CfS6HLtq9NCccyvnvDqJE"}
